{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-beer-cologne-dusseldorf-dortmund/audio/main-259b2906ed6f.mp3","durationSec":243.192,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.82,"text":"Kölsch is a pale, clear and light beer from Cologne."},{"start":3.6,"end":7.32,"text":"It is top-fermented, which means the yeast works at warmer temperatures."},{"start":8.06,"end":10.88,"text":"That method gives the beer a fresh, slightly fruity taste."},{"start":10.88,"end":17.22,"text":"Brewing has a long history in the city, and Cologne's brewers' guild dates back to 1396."},{"start":18.44,"end":20.32,"text":"Not every beer can call itself Kölsch."},{"start":20.94,"end":28.08,"text":"In 1986, Cologne's breweries signed the Kölsch Konvention, an agreement that defines what the beer is and where it can be brewed."},{"start":28.66,"end":32.26,"text":"Later, the European Union gave the name geographical protection."},{"start":32.26,"end":36.34,"text":"So Kölsch is like Champagne: the place is part of the name."},{"start":37.12,"end":41.8,"text":"The word is also the name of the local dialect, so people joke that it is the only language you can drink."},{"start":42.52,"end":44.44,"text":"The drinking customs are just as important."},{"start":45.3,"end":48.6,"text":"Kölsch comes in a narrow 0.2-litre glass called a Stange."},{"start":49.1,"end":55.28,"text":"The waiter is called a Köbes, and he carries the glasses in a round tray called a Kranz."},{"start":55.28,"end":59.08,"text":"When your glass is empty, the Köbes usually replaces it without asking."},{"start":59.8,"end":62.06,"text":"He also marks each beer on your beer mat."},{"start":62.6,"end":65.28,"text":"To stop, you put the beer mat on top of your glass."},{"start":65.28,"end":74.32,"text":"Famous brewery pubs in the Old Town include Früh, founded in 1904, and Päffgen, founded in 1883."},{"start":75.38,"end":76.9,"text":"Why such small glasses?"},{"start":77.6,"end":81.66,"text":"The beer stays cold and fresh, and the quick refills keep the room lively."},{"start":82.94,"end":85.7,"text":"In Düsseldorf, people drink Altbier."},{"start":85.7,"end":89.76,"text":"Many visitors think \"Alt\" means old beer, but that is a mistake."},{"start":90.62,"end":97.08,"text":"\"Alt\" refers to the old way of brewing, with top-fermenting yeast, the same basic method used for Kölsch."},{"start":97.64,"end":99.4,"text":"The result is very different, though."},{"start":99.4,"end":104.86,"text":"Altbier is dark copper or brown, with a stronger malt flavour and more bitterness."},{"start":104.86,"end":110.48,"text":"Altbier is usually served in a small glass, often 0.25 litres."},{"start":110.48,"end":113.44,"text":"As in Cologne, the waiters are called Köbes."},{"start":113.44,"end":121.76,"text":"The heart of this culture is the Old Town, which locals call \"the longest bar in the world\" because it has so many pubs close together."},{"start":121.76,"end":130.6,"text":"Traditional brewery pubs there include Schumacher (1838), Füchschen (1848) and Uerige (1862)."},{"start":131.74,"end":134.58,"text":"Each one brews its own Altbier."},{"start":134.58,"end":135.78,"text":"This explains the rivalry."},{"start":136.62,"end":139.12,"text":"The two cities are only about 40 kilometres apart."},{"start":139.46,"end":144,"text":"Their beers use a similar method and have similar customs, but they look and taste different."},{"start":144.68,"end":147.84,"text":"Small differences between close neighbours often create the strongest feelings."},{"start":148.76,"end":151.6,"text":"The rivalry also appears in Carnival and football."},{"start":151.6,"end":156,"text":"Cologne is the bigger city, but Düsseldorf is the state capital."},{"start":156.6,"end":160.98,"text":"Locals often joke that you should never order Kölsch in Düsseldorf or Altbier in Cologne."},{"start":161.82,"end":164.06,"text":"Mostly, this is humour, not real hostility."},{"start":165.34,"end":166.64,"text":"Dortmund's story is different."},{"start":167.84,"end":172.14,"text":"It is a city in the Ruhr, a region that became rich from coal mining and steel."},{"start":172.82,"end":179.62,"text":"In the second half of the 1800s, many people did hard, hot work there, and local breweries grew quickly."},{"start":180.78,"end":182.98,"text":"Dortmunder Export developed in this world."},{"start":183.82,"end":192.06,"text":"It is a bottom-fermented pale lager, a little stronger than many everyday beers, with more malt and less bitterness than a Pils."},{"start":192.06,"end":196.38,"text":"The name \"Export\" shows that it was made to be sold far beyond the city."},{"start":197,"end":201.18,"text":"For a long time, Dortmund was one of the biggest brewing cities in Europe."},{"start":201.18,"end":210.3,"text":"Famous names include Dortmunder Actien-Brauerei (DAB), founded in 1868, and Dortmunder Union."},{"start":211.04,"end":213.78,"text":"You can still see this history in the Dortmunder U."},{"start":214.16,"end":221.26,"text":"This former Union brewery building has a large glowing \"U\" on its roof, and today it is a centre for art and culture."},{"start":222,"end":227.62,"text":"As heavy industry declined and Pils became more popular, Export lost much of its importance."},{"start":228.6,"end":231.6,"text":"The Ruhr's last coal mine closed in 2018."},{"start":232.74,"end":237.32,"text":"So in Dortmund, you will not find a strict glass ritual like Cologne's."},{"start":237.66,"end":242.82,"text":"The beer's meaning is in its story: it was the drink of an industrial city at work."}],"words":[{"text":"Kölsch","start":0,"end":0.4},{"text":"is","start":0.4,"end":0.54},{"text":"a","start":0.54,"end":0.68},{"text":"pale","start":0.68,"end":1},{"text":"clear","start":1.18,"end":1.42},{"text":"and","start":1.58,"end":1.72},{"text":"light","start":1.72,"end":1.92},{"text":"beer","start":1.92,"end":2.2},{"text":"from","start":2.2,"end":2.46},{"text":"Cologne","start":2.46,"end":2.82},{"text":"It","start":3.6,"end"